# The brief and the memo moved into reference/ on 7 September 2026 and are
# committed from that day on. Both were ignored at the repo root until then,
# which is how phase 14 part 7a came to commit twenty one pages generated from
# a file no clone has ever held. Source comments all over this repository cite
# the two by name and by section number, and those citations are addresses a
# reader can now open.
#   reference/careers-gftv-spec.md  the brief for the whole project
#   reference/next-steps.md         the phase memo, rewritten at each boundary
#
# The other two are unchanged: working references, not part of the deliverable,
# at the repo root on the maintainer's machine only. The theme is implemented
# in full in main-site/assets/css/theme.css, which is committed.
#   gftv-theme.md         the GFTV theme system, shared across the GFTV apps
#   gftv-official.md      the official site banner, shared across the GFTV apps
*spec.md
!reference/careers-gftv-spec.md
gftv-theme.md
gftv-official.md

# Throwaway scripts at the repo root. A phase's checks used to be written here,
# run once, and deleted; from 21 August 2026 the ones worth keeping move into
# tests/ instead, which is committed and documented in tests/README.md. Anything
# still loose at the root is genuinely scratch.
*.mjs
!tests/*.mjs
!docs-site/scripts/*.mjs
*.log
.claude
gen-*.js

# The seven at the root that are not throwaway, listed one by one rather than by
# widening either pattern above. Phase 12 part 8 found the first three of them
# ignored while the root README told a reader to run them, which is the same
# failure that pass exists to catch from the other direction: a document
# describing something a fresh clone does not have. It caught the fifth on the
# day it was written, which is the pass doing its job rather than a near miss.
#
# **The last two are phase 14 part 10e, and they were the same failure again.**
# Part 7a wrote both, committed the pages they produce, and never noticed that
# `gen-*.js` above had swallowed the scripts: the twenty one spec pages went
# into the repository with no way for a clone to regenerate or --check them,
# and this file's own memo said "two generators at the repo root, committed".
#   seed.mjs           section 17's seed script, part of the deliverable
#   gen-icons.js       every icon under main-site/, from HLC-source.png
#   gen-screenshots.js the two install screenshots in the manifest
#   gen-review.js      the Chinese round trip page, and a guard since part 4
#   gen-docs-lib.js    the docs site's copies of the portal's shared modules,
#                      phase 13 part 1. Without it a clone cannot rebuild
#                      docs-site/api/ and cannot check that it is current.
#   gen-spec-pages.js  the brief as twenty one pages, phase 14 part 7a
#   gen-memo-pages.js  the memo as nine pages, phase 14 part 10e
!seed.mjs
!gen-icons.js
!gen-screenshots.js
!gen-review.js
!gen-docs-lib.js
!gen-spec-pages.js
!gen-memo-pages.js

# Generated review sheet for the Chinese copy. Regenerate instead of committing.
zh-review.html

# Theme captures from tests/capture-themes.mjs. Twenty screenshots that go stale
# the next time a colour token moves, so they are regenerated rather than kept.
theme-shots/

# Throwaway postings so the job board has something to render during
# development. Not a migration: unnumbered, never recorded in
# gftvjobs_migrations, and it carries its own delete block. The real seed
# script is phase 12's and is part of the deliverable.
migrations/dev-seed-jobs.sql

# Environment. .env.example is tracked on purpose, everything else is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.pnpm-store/

# Vercel
.vercel/
.vercel_build_output/

# The docs site's build, phase 13 part 5. `node docs-site/scripts/build.js`
# writes both, at deploy time and before a local preview, and neither is a
# source file: dist/ is everything that project serves, and api/_generated/ is
# what the build leaves for the functions to read. Committing either would be
# committing a copy of the content trees that can disagree with them.
docs-site/dist/
docs-site/api/_generated/

# Python, for telegram-bot/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Bot local state. Supabase is the shared source of truth, SQLite is not.
telegram-bot/*.session
telegram-bot/*.session-journal
telegram-bot/*.sqlite
telegram-bot/*.sqlite3
telegram-bot/*.db

# The gated image fixture, written and removed by tests/phase13-test.mjs.
# It is the only way to exercise 16e's authenticated image path: a gated page
# with an image on it has to exist for the length of the run. The suite deletes
# both, so these two lines only matter when a run is interrupted.
#
# **It stays a .png**, and phase 14 part 8 is when that stopped being an
# accident. Every .webp beside a gated page is one of 16g's screenshots and the
# build refuses one that no manifest entry claims; a fixture named after a real
# shot would collide with the file a capture run commits. So the fixture is the
# one image type on this site that is not a screenshot, which is also what keeps
# it out of the manifest's way.
docs-site/api/_content/admin/example.png
docs-site/api/_content/admin/example-shot.md

# Playwright, docs-site/scripts/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
